Z||000006||88formula||10-05-2001||05:00 PM||||Numbers are similar because the camshafts are very similar especially when the Cran 2030 has more lift. The stock camshaft looks like this on my program in a 2.8-liter engine. <P>RPM HORSEPOWER TORQUE<BR>2000 59.775116 156.909683<BR>2500 77.699463 163.168869<BR>3000 98.850517 172.988403<BR>3500 116.176170 174.264252<BR>4000 129.179886 169.548599<BR>4500 135.379700 157.942993<BR>5000 134.807846 141.548233<BR>5500 124.876320 119.200127<BR>6000 109.653877 95.947144<P>Here is a stock 3.4 with stock camshaft.<P>2000 74.839790 196.454453<BR>2500 94.390236 198.219498<BR>3000 117.973602 206.453812<BR>3500 136.811050 205.216568<BR>4000 150.910355 198.069839<BR>4500 159.495956 186.078613<BR>5000 162.414505 170.535233<BR>5500 158.986481 151.759811<BR>6000 148.987030 130.363663<P>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 10-05-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 10-05-2001).]||||reg||1
